templates.instructions:
Place at the path above (or in a project-local `.gemini/settings.json`). Gemini CLI's settings.json does not have an `env` block — export the two API-key env vars in your shell (or in `~/.gemini/.env`, which the CLI auto-loads):

```
GEMINI_API_KEY={{api_key}}
GOOGLE_GEMINI_BASE_URL={{base_url}}
```

{{#unless forward_auth}}The default model is pinned to `{{model_alias}}` in `settings.json`, so a bare `gemini -p "..."` uses it — override per run with `--model`. {{else}}This is a BYOK setup — set `GEMINI_API_KEY` to your own Google key (the gateway forwards it upstream) and your own models pass through; pick one per run with `gemini -p "..." --model <model>`. {{/unless}}Run with `gemini -p "..." --approval-mode yolo`. Usage statistics to Google and the update check are off (`privacy.usageStatisticsEnabled`, `general.enableAutoUpdate`, `general.enableAutoUpdateNotification`); an admin who wants them back can edit this template.

templates.body:
{
  "privacy": { "usageStatisticsEnabled": false },
  "general": { "enableAutoUpdate": false, "enableAutoUpdateNotification": false },
  "security": { "auth": { "selectedType": "gemini-api-key" } }{{#unless forward_auth}},
  "model": { "name": "{{model_alias}}" }{{/unless}}{{#if mcp_servers}},
  "mcpServers": {
{{#each mcp_servers}}    "{{slug}}": {
      "httpUrl": "{{url}}",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer {{api_key}}" }
    }{{#unless @last}},{{/unless}}
{{/each}}  }{{/if}}
}
